infographic compare-quadrant-quarter-simple-card
data
  title PACELC: the trade-off in every cell
  desc If Partition (PA/PC) choose A vs C — that is CAP. Else, normal operation (EL/EC), choose Latency vs C.
  compares
    - label PC — partition, pick Consistency
      desc Refuse stale answers to stay linearizable. Sacrifices availability while the network is split (CP).
    - label PA — partition, pick Availability
      desc Answer with possibly-stale data to stay up. Sacrifices consistency while the network is split (AP).
    - label EC — no partition, pick Consistency
      desc Coordinate every read (leader or quorum) for freshness — pays latency. Spanner, single-leader SQL.
    - label EL — no partition, pick Latency
      desc Read the nearest replica fast — may be stale. DynamoDB, Cassandra (PA/EL) live here.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #6366f1 #14b8a6
